	(text "ERC-clean means this drawing is consistent with itself. It does not mean the board works, and the two are different claims.\nEverything below is unmeasured. Drawing it neatly closes none of it:\n\n   V-084    the BT817's pixel clock and sync polarity against the actual panel. Not measured.\n   Q-308    the oil-temperature sender, and with it IC07's pull-up value. No part chosen, so that resistor carries a question\n            mark and not a number - a footprint with a '?' is honest, a plausible value would not be.\n   D-261    the IC01 and IC03 sender curves - three-point reads on the senders IN THE CAR, not from a datasheet.\n   IC04     LM393 against H11L1 is a bench result, not a preference. The hysteresis values here are derived on this sheet.\n   layout   every module and socket pin NUMBER. Functional pins are named; numbers are ordinal and are fixed at F2.\n\nScope. Schematic only, and there is no .kicad_pcb in this folder on purpose: fabricating a carrier has a lead time, a cost and a\nrevision cycle, which makes it BIG by CLAUDE.md section 3 and therefore a block before any time goes into a layout - not an\nassumption that follows from a schematic existing. The carrier can be protoboard for bring-up.\n\nThe harness is not here and never will be. Gauge, colour, bundles, cavities and cut lengths are the record's job and KiCad has no\nmodel for any of them. DP-ICU-A and DP-ICU-B appear on this sheet only as pins on the board edge; what is on the other side of\nthem belongs to cavities.csv, and if this sheet and a row ever disagree, the row is right."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 612.14 21.59 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.3 1.3)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1c136d2f-1c71-40d9-b1a2-1b96adb4f854")
	)
