	(text "500 kbps. NO termination on this board: D-079's far-end 120 ohm moved to the dash\nnode when the engine-bay drop was released (D-318 -> D-346). The common-mode choke\nis a DNP footprint for that same reason - the field says so, not a comment."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 396.24 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "22dbb2e4-1784-476c-bf91-ef76b3d3c71f")
	)
	(text "BAT54S is a SERIES pair, A - COM - K, and the direction is the whole point: COM carries the signal, A goes to GROUND so a negative\nexcursion is caught by GND - COM, and K goes to +3V3 so a positive one is caught by COM - +3V3. Drawn the other way round it clamps\nnothing and puts a diode path from +3V3 to ground through the sender. The first pass of this sheet had it backwards; the drawing is\nwhat found it, which is the argument for drawing it (README, 'Why a schematic at all')."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 350.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.3 1.3)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "266a4b33-35c4-49bc-abe6-36f3cb7c2cf4")
	)
	(text "ANALOG IN - one stage, drawn nine times"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 10.16 204.47 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.2 3.2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "284bd7fc-cfb8-4d90-9ef6-79c825889846")
	)
	(text "Trailing coil negative primary: hundreds of volts of inductive kick (luxury D-304). 2 pulses per revolution.\nThe comparator sits on +5 V DELIBERATELY. Its common-mode input range stops about 1.5 V under its supply,\nso on 3.3 V the 5.1 V zener node would clip and the tach would read nothing above idle. That is the fact\nwhich is invisible in prose and obvious in a drawing, and it is the whole argument for drawing this."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 394.97 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.25 1.25)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2a8ce12f-316d-438e-a926-29b14be226ce")
	)
