	)
	(text "IC21 ribbons to the BT817 board, then a TFP410-class encoder and the 1920 x 720 bar's scaler,\nall of it off this board (chain ii, D-269). The backlight's 12 V comes from J2 and never from\nthis header. V-084 confirms the pixel clock and sync polarity against the real panel; nothing\non this sheet does, and drawing it neatly does not close it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 548.64 388.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.25 1.25)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9da56f81-88ce-4c71-936d-635aa6259688")
	)
	(text "The reference and the feedback are DERIVED ON THIS SHEET and are not in the record: 5 x 12/51 = 1.18 V at the reference,\nand 1.2 M against the 200 k source gives 3.3 x 200/1400 = 0.47 V of hysteresis, which is the 'about 0.5 V' the record asks for.\nThey are a proposal, not a fact. Whether an LM393 or an H11L1 opto goes here is a BENCH RESULT (icu_channels IC04) and\nnothing drawn here settles whether this stage survives a trailing coil at 6000 rpm. If it picks up noise, the opto replaces it all."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 462.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.25 1.25)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "adb4b73b-8116-4738-9a19-01553bc259fa")
	)
