				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d61eac72-570c-40f2-8ea6-c3c645926824")
	)
	(text "J8A pulls the node to +3V3 for an open-collector sensor. J8B makes a 10 k / 4.7 k divider\nfor a push-pull output, which lands at 12 x 4.7/14.7 = 3.84 V - above the rail, which is\nexactly why the BAT54S is there and is not optional. Pulses per mile is a config value,\ntrued once against a measured mile (D-272)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 304.8 452.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.25 1.25)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "da227a85-aaf3-47f4-b0e9-11948002867a")
	)
	(text "the PWM-dimmed O20 bus the display follows"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 935.99 224.79 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e4d9fc2f-e658-40f1-9735-7e017e5ff32a")
	)
	(text " 4  IC04 tach - shielded"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 8.89 267.716 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e6864c6f-47f2-4387-9d4d-c0e5d203372f")
	)
	(text "The jumpers are why this board outlives the 12A (D-262): open J1 or J3 and the same x0.4 divider reads a 0-5 V transducer instead of a\nresistive sender. J7 is a footprint only - there is no oil-temperature sender on the 12A and no conductor run for one (D-264), so\nDP-ICU-B 7 carries a sealing plug and the swap's rebuilt leg lands there."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 360.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.3 1.3)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "eb2b452e-e18e-463f-8ef0-50e4ff0cf072")
	)
